## CMS

**Thirteen collections, not six.** Webflow's `manifest.json` names only the six with a detail
template; the other seven appear only inside lists on other pages and are invisible there. Ids and
field schemas are in [migration-scripts/webflow/collections.mjs](migration-scripts/webflow/collections.mjs).

Pulled verbatim to `migration/raw/` (gitignored, re-pullable):

| Collection | Items | Live | Route |
|---|---|---|---|
| `tour` | 102 | **29** | `/tour/<slug>` |
| `tourCategory` | 11 | 11 | `/tours/<slug>` |
| `area` | 17 | 15 | `/area/<slug>` |
| `tag` | 4 | 4 | `/tag/<slug>` |
| `review` | 12 | 11 | `/reviews/<slug>` |
| `news` | 2 | 1 | `/news/<slug>` |
| `island` | 2 | 2 | — |
| `pickUp` | 5 | 5 | — |
| `special` | 5 | 5 | — |
| `featured` | 4 | 2 | — |
| `faq` | **0** | 0 | — |
| `alert` | 1 | **0** | — |
| `cancellationPolicy` | 1 | **0** | — |

Live counts reconcile exactly to the URL inventory above.

### What the read found

- **`tour` is 71% dead weight** — 102 items, 29 live. The 73 archived/draft items are the single
  biggest exclusion and must be dropped at convert time, by Webflow's own
  `isArchived`/`isDraft` flags rather than by any list of slugs.
- **Three collections are empty shells.** `faq` has no items at all — despite a `/faq` page, so
  that page's content is static HTML, not CMS. `alert` and `cancellationPolicy` hold one
  unpublished item each. All three are candidates for wholesale exclusion.
- **A populated field that nothing renders: `tour.pricing-section-intro-text`.** Set on four live
  tours, rendered on no page on the site. The content is real copy, and two of the four are
  **stale** — "This rate is applied till end of SEP 2025", "☆From Sep to Mar 2025". A
  field-by-field importer would publish expired pricing notes.
- **Five fields are never set on any live item**: `tour.halal`, `area.featured`, `area.seq`,
  `tag.description`, `tag.text`, `special.pos`. `area.seq` and `special.pos` being empty means
  neither collection has a working order field — area ordering comes from somewhere else and has
  to be found.
- **Two mechanisms for one concept.** `area.island` is a Reference to the `island` collection;
  `tour.island` is a plain Option field. They must not be modelled as one thing without deciding
  which wins.
- **The apparent duplicate fields are not duplicates.** Checked by searching every archived page
  for each field's value: `tourCategory.brief` renders in the nav on *every* page,
  `brief-text` only on the category page intro, `text` only in its body. Same for
  `review.brief` / `general-brief` / `full`. All live, three distinct roles each — none to exclude.
- **`special` barely surfaces.** One of the five is a homepage banner (`homepage-banner` switch
  plus hero image and link); the rest appear only in the `/sitemap` page listing. One
  `special.text` is a single affiliate link carrying a referral code; another is two
  zero-width-character paragraphs, i.e. empty.

### Fixture candidates

Real excerpts for the converter tests (`migration/fixtures/`), each chosen because it breaks a
naive conversion: `id=""` attribute noise on `<p>`, paragraphs containing only a zero-width
joiner, and `<strong>` nested inside a `<p id="">`. All three are in
`tour.pricing-section-intro-text` alone.

## Shell

- **Header** — one unclassed top-level `div` holding `.site-bar` (EN/JA switcher), `.brand-section`, `.alert-bar`, `.navigation-bar.w-nav`.
- **Footer** — up to three top-level divs: `.subscribe`, `.footer`, `.copyright-section`. **Composition varies per template** — `/area/*` has no `.copyright-section`, `/reviews/*` and `/news/*` have no `.subscribe`. The punch-out must tolerate absence rather than assume the set.
- `/tour/*` wraps the entire page in `div.page-wrapper`; every other template does not.
- `/data/llms` has no shell at all.
- **The shell is CMS-driven**: ~9 `.w-dyn-list` wrappers live in the header and footer on every page.

## Assets

- **609 distinct Webflow-hosted asset URLs** across the 91 pages and the ported stylesheet
  (604 on Webflow's CDN, 5 on its CloudFront). All must be localised before cut-over.
- **No `@font-face` WOFF2 files** — type comes from Google Fonts via `webfont.js`. The usual
  font trap does not apply here; Google Fonts stays external (known gap).
- Webflow CDN filenames in the CSS contain `%20(1)`-style parentheses, so the HTML and CSS
  URL patterns must differ as the process requires.
- **A third trap, new on this site:** Webflow writes inline backgrounds as
  `style="background-image:url(&quot;https://…&quot;)"`. A scanner that does not decode entities
  before matching runs past the closing `&quot;` and captures a URL ending in `&quot;)`. Webflow
  answers those with **403**, so they read as dead assets rather than as the local bug they are —
  127 of them on the first pass here. Decode entities first, then apply the per-context
  terminator. Worth folding into the process notes.

